[38;2;124;124;124mWe have:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $K$ is an imaginary quadratic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $E$ is an elliptic curve over $\mathbb{Q}$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $p \neq l$ are primes where $E$ has good reduction[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $p$ splits in $K/\mathbb{Q}$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $l$ stays inert in $K/\mathbb{Q}$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $K_l$ is the localization of $K$ at the place $l$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mQuestion: Is there always an isomorphism $H^1(K_l, E)_{p^n} \to E(K_l)/p^n [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mE(K_l)$, at least for large enough $n$?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFirst, since $l$ is inert in $K$, $K_l$ is an unramified quadratic extension of [0m[38;2;124;124;124m$\mathbb{Q}_l$. So $K_l$ is a local field, a degree 2 unramified extension of $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{Q}_l$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, $p \neq l$, so we're looking at $p$-primary torsion in the cohomology and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe $p$-power Selmer-type quotient, where $p$ is different from the residue [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcharacteristic $l$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me recall the Kummer sequence. For an abelian variety $A$ over a local field[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$F$, the Kummer sequence gives:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$0 \to A(F)/nA(F) \to H^1(F, A[n]) \to H^1(F, A)[n] \to 0$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $H^1(F, A)[n]$ is the cokernel of $A(F)/nA(F) \to H^1(F, A[n])$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe question asks about $H^1(K_l, E)_{p^n}$, the $p^n$-torsion of $H^1(K_l, E)$,[0m[38;2;124;124;124mversus $E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, let me re-read. The question is about whether there's an isomorphism [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$H^1(K_l, E)_{p^n} \to E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFrom the Kummer sequence with $n = p^n$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$0 \to E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l) \to H^1(K_l, E[p^n]) \to H^1(K_l, E)[p^n] \to 0$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l)$ injects into $H^1(K_l, E[p^n])$ and $H^1(K_l, E)[p^n]$ is[0m[38;2;124;124;124mthe quotient.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor these two to be isomorphic, we'd need $H^1(K_l, E[p^n]) \cong E(K_l)/p^n [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mE(K_l) \oplus H^1(K_l, E)[p^n]$ and the map to be an isomorphism... Actually, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe question is asking whether $H^1(K_l, E)_{p^n} \cong E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNote: $H^1(K_l, E)_{p^n}$ means the $p^n$-torsion subgroup, i.e., elements [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mkilled by $p^n$. This is $H^1(K_l, E)[p^n]$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the question is: is $H^1(K_l, E)[p^n] \cong E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l)$?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFrom the Kummer sequence, these are related but generally not isomorphic. The [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mKummer sequence gives:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$0 \to E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l) \to H^1(K_l, E[p^n]) \to H^1(K_l, E)[p^n] \to 0$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo for them to be isomorphic, we'd need the middle term to split in a specific [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mway, or more precisely, we'd need $E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l) \cong H^1(K_l, E)[p^n]$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about the structure of these groups.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $p \neq l$, $E$ has good reduction at $l$, and $K_l$ is an unramified [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mextension of $\mathbb{Q}_l$ of degree 2.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor an elliptic curve over a local field $F$ with good reduction, and $p$ not [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mequal to the residue characteristic:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe group $E(F)$ fits into the exact sequence:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$0 \to \hat{E}(\mathfrak{m}_F) \to E(F) \to \tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_F) \to 0$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mwhere $\hat{E}$ is the formal group and $\tilde{E}$ is the reduction.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $p \neq l$, the formal group $\hat{E}(\mathfrak{m}_F)$ is a pro-$l$ group,[0m[38;2;124;124;124mso it has no $p$-torsion. Thus:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$E(F)/p^n E(F) \cong \tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_F)/p^n \tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_F)$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $\tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_F)$ is finite, $E(F)/p^n E(F) \cong \tilde{E}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(\mathbb{F}_F)[p^n]$ (the $p^n$-torsion in the reduction).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, more precisely: $\tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_F)$ is a finite abelian group. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$E(F)/p^n E(F) \cong \tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_F)/p^n \tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_F) \cong [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_F)[p^n]$ (since for a finite abelian group $G$, $G/p^n G [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\cong G[p^n]$).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually that's not quite right in general. For a finite abelian group $G$, $G/[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mp^nG \cong G[p^n]$ only if... hmm, let me think. If $G = \mathbb{Z}/[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mm\mathbb{Z}$, then $G/p^n G = \mathbb{Z}/\gcd(m, p^n)\mathbb{Z}$ and $G[p^n] = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\{x \in G : p^n x = 0\} = \mathbb{Z}/\gcd(m, p^n)\mathbb{Z}$. So yes, for cyclic[0m[38;2;124;124;124mgroups they're the same, and by the structure theorem, for any finite abelian [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgroup, $G/p^n G \cong G[p^n]$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l) \cong \tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_{K_l})[p^n]$ where $\mathbb{F}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m_{K_l}$ is the residue field of $K_l$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $K_l$ is the unramified quadratic extension of $\mathbb{Q}_l$, the residue[0m[38;2;124;124;124mfield is $\mathbb{F}_{l^2}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $E(K_l)/p^n E(K_l) \cong \tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_{l^2})[p^n]$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, for $n$ large enough, $\tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_{l^2})[p^n] = \tilde{E}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(\mathbb{F}_{l^2})[p^\infty]$, which stabilizes. So for large $n$, $E(K_l)/p^n [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mE(K_l)$ stabilizes to the $p$-primary part of $\tilde{E}(\mathbb{F}_{l^2})$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow let's think about $H^1(K_l, E)[p^n]$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $p \neq l$, the $p$-cohomology is "unramified" in some sense. Let me think[0m[38;2;124;124;124mabout this more carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me use the fact that for a local field $F$ and an abelian variety [0m[38;2;124;124;124m$A/F$ with good reduction, and $p$ not equal to the residue characteristic, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthere's a relationship between $H^1(F, A)$ and the reduction.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBy the Hochschild-Serre spectral sequence (or just the standard theory), for [0m
